\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Experiments at 500-client scale (five seeds unless noted). (a) Scheduler simulation across regimes; the accuracy column is the bounded utility state of Section~\ref {sec:eval}, MB is the attempted uplink payload of admitted clients in the final round, and FedAvg refers to full-model updates at their real serialized size. (b) Solver study with $K{=}25$ and 30 instances per cell on the identical ceiling grid; the table reports heuristic objective loss relative to the grid-based DP and DP runtime.}}{24}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:scalemain}{{4}{24}{}{}{}}
